  "id": "paranoid-disorders",
  "term": "Paranoid Disorders",
  "definition": "Paranoid disorders are long-lasting mental health conditions marked by the gradual formation of fixed, persistent delusions, such as beliefs of being persecuted or a partner being unfaithful. Despite these false beliefs, the person’s thinking can otherwise remain clear and organized, and their emotions and behavior tend to fit the delusional beliefs.",
